---
description: Commit message and branching conventions. Apply when the user asks to commit, write a commit message, or open a pull request.
alwaysApply: false
---

- Conventional Commits: `type(scope): imperative summary` (feat, fix, refactor, perf, test, docs, build, ci, chore). Subject max 72 chars.
- Body explains why, not what. Add `BREAKING CHANGE:` when public APIs, env vars or schemas change.
- One logical change per commit. Suggest splitting mixed diffs.
- Show the message and ask before committing. Never `--no-verify`, never force-push, never rewrite pushed history unless explicitly asked.
